Defeated, he wonders aloud if what [[Lance]] told him about not treating his Pokémon properly is true, but refuses to give up on becoming stronger.

=====The Shifting Shutters=====
After {{ga|Silver}} leaves, there are three Rocket Grunts along the north wall. Defeat them all, then turn your attention to the three switches on the wall behind them. These switches are numbered from 1 to 3, starting with the eastern one. Each of these switches controls a different group of shutters to the south. To reset the puzzle, either flip each switch again or leave and re-enter the room.

* Flip the switches in a four-part sequence (#2, #1, #2, #3) to reach a [[Full Heal]] in the northeast room, a hidden [[Max Potion]] in the north-central room, a hidden [[Revive]] in the northwest room, and a [[Smoke Ball]] in the southwest room.
* To clear the maze, flip each switch once in descending order (#3, #2, #1). Defeat the two Burglars on the way.

After exiting the maze, defeat the female Rocket Grunt and pass through the double doors.

====Warehouse====
Go north to reach an [[Ultra Ball]], then follow the winding hallway past the first Rocket Grunt to reach a [[Max Ether]] in the southeast corner. Battle a second Rocket Grunt in the northeast, then detour up the nearby stairs; this leads to a blocked-off area in the [[Goldenrod Department Store|Department Store]]'s basement and an [[Amulet Coin]]. Continue westward to fight a third Rocket Grunt. Pick up {{TM|35|Sleep Talk}} in the interior room, then speak to the Director. After hearing about [[Team Rocket]] occupying the [[Goldenrod Radio Tower|Radio Tower]], he begs for your help and gives you a {{jo|Card Key}}. This card unlocks the shutter on the tower's third floor. Climb the northeast stairs again and take the elevator up from the basement.

===Radio Tower===
With the {{jo|Card Key}} in hand, it is time to defeat [[Team Rocket]] once and for all!

