Conceding defeat, the Rocket Executive formally disbands [[Team Rocket]], just as [[Giovanni]] did before him. The Rockets flee the building, and the Director returns a moment later. He exclaims that your courageous actions have saved Pokémon nationwide, and rewards you with a [[Clear Bell]]. He explains that there used to be a different tower at this site, but it was old and unstable. This gleaming bell was dug up during demolition to make way for the new Radio Tower. He wonders aloud if it might have some connection to {{ci|Ecruteak}}'s [[Bell Tower|Tin Tower]], then suddenly remembers overhearing a conversation between [[Team Rocket]] members. He says that they were whispering about something going on at that same tower, and suggests looking into it before leaving for his office. Pick up the [[Ultra Ball]] in the studio here, and then as you exit the tower, speak to [[DJ Mary]] on 4F (East) for a [[Pink Bow]], and the girl on 3F to get {{TM|11|Sunny Day}}.

==Ecruteak City==
===Barrier Station===
In the building at the foot of [[Bell Tower|Tin Tower]], one of the tower's caretakers informs you that a momentous event has occurred. He initially asks you to leave, but relents when he hears the [[Clear Bell]] begin ringing gently. The bell's chime is said to reflect the bearer's soul, and he believes that you may be able to make it through the tower.

As you approach the exit, you are blocked by a group known as the Wise Trio. They speak of a legend in which a Trainer with the ability to touch the souls of Pokémon is tested by a Pokémon that appears at [[Bell Tower|Tin Tower]]. They excitedly inform you that the legend has come true, as {{p|Suicune}} has appeared at the tower. The trio intends to test your worthiness to meet the beast. Between battles, they offer more insight into the local legends.

